  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and typecheck passes. I haven't run it in a browser, so it's untested visually. The scene has four parts:\n\n- **Island:** a faceted, flat-shaded terrain mesh. Each triangle has its own face normal and a height-based colour (sand, grass, rock, snow). Instanced cone and cylinder trees and rocks sit on it.\n- **Water:** a custom GLSL wave mesh with vertex waves and fresnel shading. It also has a sun glint by day and a moon glint at night. The shader uniforms for time, sun direction and daylight are updated every frame.\n- **Sky and lighting:** `sky.preetham` with stars, plus a sun and a moon directional light that move with the day/night cycle. A hemisphere light is always on, so the scene is never black. A full cycle takes 20 seconds.\n- **Camera:** a fixed perspective camera above the water that frames the whole island. I skipped the optional slow orbit.\n\nThe first frame sets `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true`.\n\nI couldn't confirm that `setUniform` takes effect on the water node, or that `setSky` takes effect on the sky each frame. I called both with optional chaining, as the docs recipes do. If either has no effect, the water would stay at its initial daytime colours and the sky would not change.",
